{"id":20686,"artist":"Mic Darling.","title":"Hills of Connemara","lyrics_plain":null,"lyrics_synced":"[00:02.02] In the hills of Connemara.\n[00:04.62] Gather up the pots and the old tin cans,\n[00:06.78] The mash, the corn, the barley and the bran.\n[00:09.23] Run like the devil from the excise man,\n[00:11.25] Keep the smoke from rising, Barney.\n[00:16.15] Keep your eyes well peeled today,\n[00:18.32] The excise men are on their way,\n[00:20.77] Searching for the mountain tay,\n[00:22.79] In the hills of Connemara.\n[00:25.38] Swinging to the left, swinging to the right,\n[00:27.55] The excise men will dance all night.\n[00:30.00] Drinkin' up the tay till the broad daylight,\n[00:32.02] In the hills of Connemara.\n[00:34.62] A gallon for the butcher and a quart for John,\n[00:36.78] And a bottle for poor old Father Tom,\n[00:39.23] Just to help the poor old dear along,\n[00:41.25] In the hills of Connemara.\n[00:45.87] Swinging to the left, swinging to the right\n[00:48.17] The excise men will dance all night.\n[00:50.48] Drinkin' up the tay till the broad daylight,\n[00:52.79] In the hills of Connemara.\n[00:55.10] Stand your ground, for it's too late,\n[00:57.55] The excise men are at the gate.\n[00:60.00] Glory be to Paddy, but they're drinkin' it straight\n[01:02.02] In the hills of Connemara.\n[01:04.62] Swinging to the left, swinging to the right,\n[01:06.78] The excise men will dance all night.\n[01:09.23] Drinkin' up the tay till the broad daylight,\n[01:11.25] In the hills of Connemara.\n[01:13.85] Swinging to the left, swinging to the right,\n[01:16.01] The excise men will dance all night.\n[01:18.46] Drinkin' up the tay till the broad daylight,\n[01:20.48] In the hills of Connemara.\n[01:22.79] In the hills of Connemara.\n","lyrics_synced_enhanced":"[00:02.01] <00:02.01>In <00:02.16>the <00:02.30>hills <00:02.59>of <00:02.88>Con <00:03.17>ne <00:03.46>ma <00:04.03>ra.\n[00:04.61] <00:04.61>Gath <00:04.75>er <00:04.90>up <00:05.04>the <00:05.19>pots <00